    "agent_last_message": "Implemented a C++20 word-count CLI in `output/` and verified it builds with:\n\n```bash\ncmake -B build && cmake --build build\n```\n\nFiles:\n- [output/main.cpp](/workspace/output/main.cpp) contains the streaming analyzer, CLI parsing, JSON writer, and exit-code handling.\n- [output/CMakeLists.txt](/workspace/output/CMakeLists.txt) builds the `wordcount` executable with C++20.\n\nBehavior covered:\n- `--input` and `--output` flags\n- line, word, character, and unique-word counts\n- top 10 words, sorted by frequency then lexicographically\n- exit code `1` for invalid invocation or unreadable input / unwritable output\n- exit code `2` for unexpected internal errors\n\nI also checked the main spec edge cases: empty file, trailing newline, whitespace-only input, case folding, and tie ordering."
